        "color": 5,
        "content": "## Half-Built — 3 gaps\n\nNine nodes, wired. The hard date expressions are done for you — study them. Three fields to fill:\n\n1. **Compute Candidates → `cand_tue`** is blank. `cand_mon` right above it is the template:\n   `={{ DateTime.fromISO($json.requested_date).plus({ days: (8 - DateTime.fromISO($json.requested_date).weekday) % 7 || 7 }).toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd') }}`\n   Monday is weekday **1** (so `1 + 7 = 8`). Tuesday is weekday **2**. Change the **8 to a 9** to land on the next Tuesday.\n2. **Requested Date Free? → condition** is hard-wired to `={{ true }}`, so every request looks free and nothing ever finds an alternate. Replace it with a real membership test: *is the requested date NOT in the busy list?*\n   `={{ !$json.busy_dates.includes($json.requested_date) }}`\n3. **Compose Reply → prompt** is blank. Write a friendly 2-3 sentence reply that branches on `{{ $json.status }}` (`confirmed` / `alternate` / `none`) and proposes `{{ $json.chosen_date }}` (a `{{ $json.chosen_weekday }}` afternoon) when offering an alternate.\n\n**Given as worked examples:** *Pick Alternate* (the Monday-then-Tuesday-else-none choice) and *Finalise* (the weekday name). No Code node anywhere."
      }
    }
